[{:db/id "q-330627/field-1/666cc561fe574046892b9e0809734f9eac4c357108d84ebd2a59387175cdafde" :answer/id #uuid "2f60a395-ae1b-5285-b8fd-906c4071aca1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.29" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330627/field-1/9249ec38b82e800720a79ba1072f7d45fcdfddce5a4914d085b8568b9b083f3a" :answer/id #uuid "8b89faa9-2317-568a-810c-cb1e53ab6b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330627/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3b6134-c475-52df-b845-3d1464ae3eed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330627/field-1/666cc561fe574046892b9e0809734f9eac4c357108d84ebd2a59387175cdafde" :answer-field/choices ["q-330627/field-1/666cc561fe574046892b9e0809734f9eac4c357108d84ebd2a59387175cdafde" "q-330627/field-1/9249ec38b82e800720a79ba1072f7d45fcdfddce5a4914d085b8568b9b083f3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330627/field-2/ad6fae648bd5d24fec24b48dbb7d3e13836de0ccd85c4d9957f8368d51d4c03e" :answer/id #uuid "e209f8c9-f0ff-59af-8985-82cbc1fb9b42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330627/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e44de73-c556-5076-bacb-a8cb1d572acd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330627/field-2/ad6fae648bd5d24fec24b48dbb7d3e13836de0ccd85c4d9957f8368d51d4c03e" :answer-field/choices ["q-330627/field-2/ad6fae648bd5d24fec24b48dbb7d3e13836de0ccd85c4d9957f8368d51d4c03e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330627" :question/id #uuid "247fbd34-ae4e-58c1-818b-930fa4d84a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-330627" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide each term of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{7\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{2})≈1.292\\,50\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}≈1.292\\,50+\\pi ≈4.434\\,09\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.29,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.43.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330627/field-1" "q-330627/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330627"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835/selection/2c2ccfdfd7b965202673a4505798f94bb3dec1aac131c47bb510c6ecab584a42" :answer/id #uuid "8eb0e5ba-bf3e-5a6b-ae7f-2ebba218c67c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16.850" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835/selection/f115131e13c06520f0f4f29ed5b909dde8adf410e2d6d8b246cc653f35696f66" :answer/id #uuid "d9fb9a89-045a-5424-a6c4-246853f976de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18.816" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835/selection/1eab6302bb36ac9003866724604713f9ba79cf3fe45d9835f2210307fc3213ff" :answer/id #uuid "f0d74397-059d-5b48-aec2-fd64b98c973a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.685" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835/selection/2df8310e4be3f1f86f7cba8fac3c97698c51fa98fd478195fe5b4882cc65594d" :answer/id #uuid "4ef69f4a-85d2-5742-864e-c7d9d1f905e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.859" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835/selection/902405a0dbb2ee323b68eca5dfe9746e2a6656f84f426dc657f8bac4dc37df63" :answer/id #uuid "9627af9e-888f-5c62-9ef9-e1b8a9220cdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11.860" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eaaf9440-6975-54a0-b0b7-458421040865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8835/selection/902405a0dbb2ee323b68eca5dfe9746e2a6656f84f426dc657f8bac4dc37df63" :answer-field/choices ["q-8835/selection/2c2ccfdfd7b965202673a4505798f94bb3dec1aac131c47bb510c6ecab584a42" "q-8835/selection/f115131e13c06520f0f4f29ed5b909dde8adf410e2d6d8b246cc653f35696f66" "q-8835/selection/1eab6302bb36ac9003866724604713f9ba79cf3fe45d9835f2210307fc3213ff" "q-8835/selection/2df8310e4be3f1f86f7cba8fac3c97698c51fa98fd478195fe5b4882cc65594d" "q-8835/selection/902405a0dbb2ee323b68eca5dfe9746e2a6656f84f426dc657f8bac4dc37df63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8835" :question/id #uuid "457eab8b-55e1-586d-b37d-d7583b92f4b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-8835" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{4}{3})=-0.927\\,295\\,218…≈-0.927\\,295\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to 6 decimal places. \n\nSince $-0.927\\,295$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=-0.927\\,295…+\\pi ≈2.214\\,297 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=-0.927\\,295…+2\\pi ≈5.355\\,890\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈2.214\\,297\\cdot 5.355\\,890≈11.860\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330495/field-1/0ab5179a643a123ebc5759e29002b95a10fa75402ca63a1ff627d27904361aec" :answer/id #uuid "e50b34f9-5701-5bf0-a0e7-ec62466b033f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330495/field-1/9ebb7a41bdb3c695a87a6c3518d522fa1aaa166b3aa1f0a71f2d4d592e45fcfe" :answer/id #uuid "3fe28804-38f4-522d-90c7-24d692d732f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330495/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "096f627c-e501-5c9d-9a75-2be8b4af0785" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330495/field-1/0ab5179a643a123ebc5759e29002b95a10fa75402ca63a1ff627d27904361aec" :answer-field/choices ["q-330495/field-1/0ab5179a643a123ebc5759e29002b95a10fa75402ca63a1ff627d27904361aec" "q-330495/field-1/9ebb7a41bdb3c695a87a6c3518d522fa1aaa166b3aa1f0a71f2d4d592e45fcfe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330495/field-2/3d03ed166000df4abc478ed2edec05f8796bcdb2dfd79651893420a90674e3f1" :answer/id #uuid "2f1b9744-6b9a-5188-ae4f-1bb29558b8f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330495/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "23d4ae52-db0c-526c-becd-d99f8063bc25" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330495/field-2/3d03ed166000df4abc478ed2edec05f8796bcdb2dfd79651893420a90674e3f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-330495/field-2/3d03ed166000df4abc478ed2edec05f8796bcdb2dfd79651893420a90674e3f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330495" :question/id #uuid "4f92d416-4a19-5cd0-a0f1-8a1e9373ff75" :question/math-academy-id "q-330495" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{8}{3})≈1.212\\,03\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\nx≈1.212\\,03+\\pi ≈4.353\\,62\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.21,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.35.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330495/field-1" "q-330495/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330495"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607/selection/84b19c2e84e71ba898aea47f08909f10dd3162f07a7a706057cb032f9fd0361e" :answer/id #uuid "032c15da-959d-52f5-890e-f2996d46c640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6\\pi }{55}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607/selection/cc02a69ed30fc2bf3f464be984be409ea0a228da64d877402fc72d4b113d67de" :answer/id #uuid "9dcd4c97-841c-5b1e-a5e1-7e6abe840952" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607/selection/9bf0dac6e6d62ac21baa15e9e1e1b872cf646950f11e8b1d0202c86aef599481" :answer/id #uuid "43063b8f-df7a-5448-bd10-557e9bf7caf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{55\\pi }{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607/selection/83849fe89d05f0a77c09873804f8b69446707b3b4f6ef5e378e748d2880d3fa8" :answer/id #uuid "275f56c1-863b-5026-818c-b03125703d6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36\\pi }{55}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607/selection/3fcbf82a8f74dfe0a77d38290001593a41b2dec205c8227085affa8869fa3c4d" :answer/id #uuid "07c041f9-f522-5183-8cb6-12c9d870ca9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36{\\pi }^{2}}{55}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "614c4d4a-9018-525c-aeea-a4954c1ee8f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-21607/selection/cc02a69ed30fc2bf3f464be984be409ea0a228da64d877402fc72d4b113d67de" :answer-field/choices ["q-21607/selection/84b19c2e84e71ba898aea47f08909f10dd3162f07a7a706057cb032f9fd0361e" "q-21607/selection/cc02a69ed30fc2bf3f464be984be409ea0a228da64d877402fc72d4b113d67de" "q-21607/selection/9bf0dac6e6d62ac21baa15e9e1e1b872cf646950f11e8b1d0202c86aef599481" "q-21607/selection/83849fe89d05f0a77c09873804f8b69446707b3b4f6ef5e378e748d2880d3fa8" "q-21607/selection/3fcbf82a8f74dfe0a77d38290001593a41b2dec205c8227085affa8869fa3c4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-21607" :question/id #uuid "7e1c09e9-6554-5dcd-aed9-01c917440de8" :question/math-academy-id "q-21607" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=x+2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{11\\pi }{6}=\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-21607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-21607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831/selection/afc492f6fb67539104001c51738c871ec23fe4a0946711aa33c81b6e24e16c1c" :answer/id #uuid "5bc5c472-d6e8-5e40-a41a-6bb6e2d031e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.156" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831/selection/28afdf74607ae4f6a629f2b61297297d2d1f418ff0a6805214b600e5d3ff604c" :answer/id #uuid "2a68f6b0-26ed-50d7-bf3c-758b5196d3cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831/selection/4b4c8344f0810f51b1279309409ce68e84e1cab94257000149da6c60d96d037f" :answer/id #uuid "0b87879d-ac03-5c2d-a111-c9bc0373e900" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.062" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831/selection/fe3c51cfa2ba7d397ce0de180059ff4ddb645134010f1c819fd119cf3b8e0f66" :answer/id #uuid "fec7db22-9de3-505e-a0c1-ad866b25b37e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.156" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831/selection/33b74ecd88eb1be9f32aff5593d569c8f52fe5442d804c15f38210aad775eb24" :answer/id #uuid "0c63f889-7581-5098-a6a9-cc5232925bf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.306" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb088d7-ab70-51b0-b357-1cedba672feb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8831/selection/fe3c51cfa2ba7d397ce0de180059ff4ddb645134010f1c819fd119cf3b8e0f66" :answer-field/choices ["q-8831/selection/afc492f6fb67539104001c51738c871ec23fe4a0946711aa33c81b6e24e16c1c" "q-8831/selection/28afdf74607ae4f6a629f2b61297297d2d1f418ff0a6805214b600e5d3ff604c" "q-8831/selection/4b4c8344f0810f51b1279309409ce68e84e1cab94257000149da6c60d96d037f" "q-8831/selection/fe3c51cfa2ba7d397ce0de180059ff4ddb645134010f1c819fd119cf3b8e0f66" "q-8831/selection/33b74ecd88eb1be9f32aff5593d569c8f52fe5442d804c15f38210aad775eb24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8831" :question/id #uuid "3f8bfbe2-b922-56e7-8c09-11a1f10461da" :question/math-academy-id "q-8831" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-5 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})=1.190\\,289\\,949…≈1.190\\,290\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $1.190\\,290$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.190\\,290.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +1.190\\,289\\,949…=4.331\\,882\\,603\\,…≈4.331\\,883\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.190\\,290\\cdot 4.331\\,883≈5.156\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a681cf28-41fa-5547-ba25-ee6a720e1a4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122673/selection/ce79539a2a3864aee65cc4be03869ce5908d0d656d32234ae7d793918b41e2e8" :answer/id #uuid "871b6304-0373-5c38-9be8-3ff814595391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9\\,892" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122673/selection/c53d5aa434fd609081732ef1b5d4a9ed8f7649e6a73de8108bf882e64d210657" :answer/id #uuid "f4079bc1-b3b2-5fcd-8b9b-0083c0657ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\,010" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122673/selection/fb2011e8e0ca7ce8d2141a48ea3f554a6cc38a94b19f4dd92ee2905c6c217fef" :answer/id #uuid "72e352ed-257b-5929-b793-ff50dc14a93f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8\\,000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122673/selection/d2eb0a1b4d51ef27eae956e9f3393d6aa8181fe1faff55b613c3d3d4a26278e8" :answer/id #uuid "4d8cfb00-f8ac-5efe-9911-f1f11307c39a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,487" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122673/selection/3fd1ae0eac01f37a0d48c35d9c1799579a9b4f4b89c7bc1ad7e20218696