\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)≈{80.538}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${80.538}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={80.538}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract ${180}^{∘}$ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={80.538}^{∘}-{180}^{∘}≈-{99.462}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $80.538\\cdot (-99.462)≈-8\\,010.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122673/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873/selection/7c227b2a513e666bd95a9e37ba5e6806ace8588a88c98b1856b1ab5b38c9bb65" :answer/id #uuid "8046f224-b274-5617-a4d0-eac096290dcf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.74" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873/selection/b7b68bbda918eaa251ee715b178edcc2e9a492ee8d87334c1716f1e9cff8126e" :answer/id #uuid "0b3b9567-4608-56b3-9335-8ff92260b844" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873/selection/d98f24cbb1838278306392d00a86dd4e75adfe7793012c33ba0b1df8490cbe95" :answer/id #uuid "31019fc4-6c7f-5dc2-84bd-3f7452a605b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5.86" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873/selection/2110b4ed38d4a760ad8dcd9409577e66b8f9eb60037b63362524fadbb37ecea7" :answer/id #uuid "6f7b93e0-98cf-5be2-8a42-0aacddac3112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873/selection/0564e2a07957ffc4bd0cc8fbc7290c48138abf779d15c6622cae01afd110195f" :answer/id #uuid "ba1bb589-53b5-5c64-82e5-e9ea1b169814" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "67fd613a-0346-5af5-a6d2-ac898103d555" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8873/selection/2110b4ed38d4a760ad8dcd9409577e66b8f9eb60037b63362524fadbb37ecea7" :answer-field/choices ["q-8873/selection/7c227b2a513e666bd95a9e37ba5e6806ace8588a88c98b1856b1ab5b38c9bb65" "q-8873/selection/b7b68bbda918eaa251ee715b178edcc2e9a492ee8d87334c1716f1e9cff8126e" "q-8873/selection/d98f24cbb1838278306392d00a86dd4e75adfe7793012c33ba0b1df8490cbe95" "q-8873/selection/2110b4ed38d4a760ad8dcd9409577e66b8f9eb60037b63362524fadbb37ecea7" "q-8873/selection/0564e2a07957ffc4bd0cc8fbc7290c48138abf779d15c6622cae01afd110195f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8873" :question/id #uuid "14075095-b35c-5376-9922-d351dd7229a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-8873" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-0.463\\,647…≈-0.463\\,65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSince $-0.463\\,65$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.463\\,65.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-0.463\\,65…+\\pi ≈2.677\\,95\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈-0.463\\,65\\cdot 2.677\\,95≈-1.24\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8873/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8873"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870/selection/342735ae3ee1cdd49b787a7deb8d8ac0069f12ec644c41abdbbac0f118f45cee" :answer/id #uuid "beafe223-41aa-5a15-8822-699b56b7d26a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.407" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870/selection/eb04f4104bbf79c4eba80507f53839843c438a22eb8ff129ec70417203860704" :answer/id #uuid "93fd7450-b01c-59be-89a6-bd562e182cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.157" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870/selection/81eb4ee3948fa35ea350dde5778aa602e6d0c241944d4c06c8d573ea5b7e0219" :answer/id #uuid "ad2d6613-073e-5e81-b5a3-223e6c163096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.367" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870/selection/1534f3c225f601360207dbc1f63f0a3c9ebf96ecc07d1328852b5b8e018cecfc" :answer/id #uuid "6d2892c1-8988-5b1e-b341-ab4a1fa46866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.787" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870/selection/896fb8b3f3c64e87fd36a3a33e6fbd7e37afb9982a859661e01af7899a4f0919" :answer/id #uuid "7f214933-2cc3-58ac-b522-713ec221fbf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.499" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "675a29db-136d-52db-9f80-5562f0f8c1f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8870/selection/342735ae3ee1cdd49b787a7deb8d8ac0069f12ec644c41abdbbac0f118f45cee" :answer-field/choices ["q-8870/selection/342735ae3ee1cdd49b787a7deb8d8ac0069f12ec644c41abdbbac0f118f45cee" "q-8870/selection/eb04f4104bbf79c4eba80507f53839843c438a22eb8ff129ec70417203860704" "q-8870/selection/81eb4ee3948fa35ea350dde5778aa602e6d0c241944d4c06c8d573ea5b7e0219" "q-8870/selection/1534f3c225f601360207dbc1f63f0a3c9ebf96ecc07d1328852b5b8e018cecfc" "q-8870/selection/896fb8b3f3c64e87fd36a3a33e6fbd7e37afb9982a859661e01af7899a4f0919"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8870" :question/id #uuid "0ded74ca-6dcb-53b6-9e83-9f98736a964d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8870" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{16\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{16\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 4\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-16 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =16 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4)=1.325\\,817\\,663…≈1.325\\,818\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $1.325\\,818$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.325\\,818.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=1.325\\,817\\,663…-\\pi =-1.815\\,774\\,989…≈-1.815\\,775\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.325\\,818\\cdot (-1.815\\,775)≈-2.407\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8870/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8870"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330590/field-1/cc3b2e09f31260936dbe1c238f26a8ac50d2b8e0624abc8cba23b63f94021d56" :answer/id #uuid "02501101-4df0-5fff-a801-7fff985f15e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.95" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330590/field-1/b3365381c0f329fb9bfaa57b6a7b15c62b274595f02a293b78f31b6d6dd0a466" :answer/id #uuid "3d607832-040d-5837-bd6e-91fc0461dea4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330590/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "226e297d-0a17-5b36-8add-b9e44a46837b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330590/field-1/cc3b2e09f31260936dbe1c238f26a8ac50d2b8e0624abc8cba23b63f94021d56" :answer-field/choices ["q-330590/field-1/cc3b2e09f31260936dbe1c238f26a8ac50d2b8e0624abc8cba23b63f94021d56" "q-330590/field-1/b3365381c0f329fb9bfaa57b6a7b15c62b274595f02a293b78f31b6d6dd0a466"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330590/field-2/d62f52881cb40cd6318e8ea86d7517b91be6cb0c54a3836839bfff056a7e9d26" :answer/id #uuid "580a6509-097c-5f64-a4c9-eb13d6530e70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330590/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2131e877-88eb-5c75-b22d-a76d1b1e5f71" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330590/field-2/d62f52881cb40cd6318e8ea86d7517b91be6cb0c54a3836839bfff056a7e9d26" :answer-field/choices ["q-330590/field-2/d62f52881cb40cd6318e8ea86d7517b91be6cb0c54a3836839bfff056a7e9d26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330590" :question/id #uuid "391ef030-a808-5483-bfcf-8d5d0b810584" :question/math-academy-id "q-330590" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $-\\pi \\le x<\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =5 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})≈1.190\\,29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find another solution in the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi )$, we subtract $\\pi :$\n\n$$\nx≈1.190\\,29-\\pi ≈-1.951\\,30\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈-1.95,\\,{x}_{2}≈1.19.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330590/field-1" "q-330590/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf1a53c0-e652-5732-9d5a-5aad004c2676"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8876"] :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract $\\pi $ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}=-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6192"] :question/problem "Calculate, in degrees to the nearest degree, the solutions to the equation $5\\sin x = -7\\cos x$ for $0^\\circ \\leq x < 360^\\circ.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide each term of the equation by $\\cos x$ and use the identity $\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-\\frac{7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-\\frac{7\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ 5\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =-7 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\tan x = -\\dfrac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nThe length of the interval for $x$ is $2\\pi$, so we will likely require $2$ solutions. \n\nWe can immediately calculate the principal value $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan\\left(-\\dfrac{7}{5}\\right) \\approx -54.46\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the domain $0^\\circ \\leq x < 360^\\circ.$ To get a value that's inside the domain, we add $180^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{7}{5})+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈-{54.46}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={125.54}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the other solution inside the given interval, we add $180^\\circ$ to $x_1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{125.54}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={305.54}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solutions, rounded to the nearest degree, are $x= 126^\\circ, 306^\\circ.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6196"] :question/problem "Calculate, in degrees to the nearest degree, the solutions to the equation $3\\sin x + 12\\cos x = 0$ for $-180^\\circ <  x \\leq 180^\\circ.$" :question/worked-solution "We divide each term of the equation by $\\cos x$ and use the identity $\\tan x = \\dfrac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{12\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{12\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+12 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\tan x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-12 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can immediately calculate the principal value $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx = \\arctan(-4) \\approx -75.96^\\circ\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the given domain, our first solution is $x_1 = -75.96^\\circ.$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we *add* $180^\\circ.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈-{75.96}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={104.04}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solutions, rounded to the nearest degree, are $x= -76^\\circ, 104^\\circ.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
